// A pickup: the piece's first bar a quarter long on both staves, the right hand's an eighth rest
// and an eighth, the left hand's an eighth rest only (its other eighth a spacer: the page shows one
// rest, as MuseScore hides the other -- kinkel19-6). The second system's printed number, 3, is the
// count less one (the pickup is bar 0). The last bar completes the pickup, a half note long. Read
// back, omr.lys opens its section with "partial 4", the left hand's pickup is "r8 s8", and the short
// last bar has no todo. lysc png --scale 5.6.
octave absolute
paper { breaksOnly }
time 3/4
key f major
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
score { grandStaff { staff rh staff lh } }
section Piece {
  partial 4
  rh {
    r8 c''8 |
    f''4 e''4 d''4 |
    c''2 a'4 | break
    bes'4 g'4 e'4 |
    f'2 |
  }
  lh {
    s8 r8 |
    f4 a4 c'4 |
    f2. | break
    c4 e4 g4 |
    f,2 |
  }
}
form { ~Piece }
